IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch2-surplus-and-floor`

-- Tests of Part 6, Chapter 2: regulation 54A (surplus earnings), 62 (minimum income floor), 63 (start-up period) and 64 (gainful
-- self-employment). Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text and written beside the assertion.

§ `Regulation 54A -- surplus earnings`

-- (6): the relevant threshold is the nil UC threshold plus 300.
#ASSERT `reg 54A(6) — the relevant threshold` 1000 EQUALS 1300
#ASSERT `reg 54A(6) — the relevant threshold` 0 EQUALS 300

GIVEN award IS A BOOLEAN
      terminated IS A DATE
      first IS A DATE
      entitled IS A BOOLEAN
      final IS A NUMBER
      earlier IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      violence IS A BOOLEAN
      joint IS A BOOLEAN
      singles IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      different IS A BOOLEAN
      apportioned IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Claim considered under regulation 54A`
`test surplus claim` award terminated first entitled final earlier violence joint singles different apportioned MEANS
    `Claim considered under regulation 54A` WITH
        `the claimant, or either of joint claimants, had an award of universal credit (the old award)` IS award
        `date on which the old award terminated` IS terminated
        `first day in respect of which the claim is made` IS first
        `the claimant has not, or neither of joint claimants has, been entitled to universal credit since the old award terminated` IS entitled
        `total earned income in the month that would have been the final assessment period for the old award, had it not terminated` IS final
        `nil UC threshold` IS 1000
        `total earned income in the month that would have been the first assessment period in relation to each earlier claim since the old award terminated` IS earlier
        `the claimant has, or had at the time the old award terminated, recently been a victim of domestic violence` IS violence
        `first joint claim by members of a couple each of whom had an old award` IS joint
        `surplus earnings of each member of the couple that would have been treated as earned income had they each claimed as a single person` IS singles
        `single claim after an award or claim as a joint claimant, or joint claim after an award or claim as a member of a different couple` IS different
        `portion of the original surplus or adjusted surplus apportioned to the claim by the Secretary of State` IS apportioned

-- The base claim: the old award ended on 31 May 2026, the claim starts on 5 August 2026, the final month's total earned income was
-- 1,700 against a relevant threshold of 1,300.
`test first claim` MEANS `test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `reg 54A(1) — this regulation applies to the claim` `test first claim`
-- (3)(a): the first claim: the original surplus, the excess of 1,700 over 1,300: 400.
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` `test first claim` EQUALS JUST 400

-- (3)(b): the second claim: 400 plus the first claim's first-month earned income (1,000) is 1,400, exceeding 1,300 by 100.
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 (LIST 1000) FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 100
-- A first-month earned income of 900 gives 400 + 900 - 1,300 = 0: nothing is left to carry.
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 (LIST 900) FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 0
-- A first-month earned income of 800 would give a negative figure (-100): "the amount, if any" is nil.
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 (LIST 800) FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 0
-- (3)(c): the third claim: 100 + 1,300 - 1,300 = 100.
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 (LIST 1000, 1300) FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 100
-- (3)(d): the fourth claim: the same again, 100; the fifth: 100 + 1,400 - 1,300 = 200.
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 (LIST 1000, 1300, 1300) FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 (LIST 1000, 1300, 1300, 1400) FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 200
-- A sixth claim since the old award terminated: the text provides nothing (fork F-A2).
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 (LIST 1000, 1300, 1300, 1400, 1500) FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1)(a): terminated on 5 February 2026, the claim starts 5 August 2026: 5 February plus six months is 5 August, included (fork F-A3).
#ASSERT `reg 54A(1) — this regulation applies to the claim` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 2 5) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING)
-- A day earlier it is more than six months before: the regulation does not apply and there is no surplus.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 54A(1) — this regulation applies to the claim` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 2 4) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING))
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 2 4) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 0
-- An award that terminates after the claim's first day is not an "old award" for the claim.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 54A(1) — this regulation applies to the claim` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 8 6) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING))
-- (1)(a) no old award; (1)(b) entitled to universal credit since.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 54A(1) — this regulation applies to the claim` (`test surplus claim` FALSE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 54A(1) — this regulation applies to the claim` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) FALSE 1700 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING))
-- (1)(c): the final month's earned income must EXCEED the relevant threshold: 1,300 does not; 1,300.01 does, giving a surplus of 0.01.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 54A(1) — this regulation applies to the claim` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1300 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING))
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1300 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1300.01 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 0.01
-- (5): a victim of domestic violence: no surplus earnings are taken into account.
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 EMPTY TRUE FALSE EMPTY FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 0
-- (4)(a): the first joint claim where each had an old award: the amounts each would have had as a single person are aggregated: 200 + 150 = 350.
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 EMPTY FALSE TRUE (LIST 200, 150) FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 350
-- (4)(b): apportioned as the Secretary of State determines: 120 once determined, NOTHING until then.
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY TRUE (JUST 120)) EQUALS JUST 120
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The apportionment rules apply only where regulation 54A applies.
#ASSERT `reg 54A — the surplus earnings treated as earned income` (`test surplus claim` TRUE (YMD 2026 2 4) (YMD 2026 8 5) TRUE 1700 EMPTY FALSE FALSE EMPTY TRUE (JUST 120)) EQUALS JUST 0

-- (6): total earned income: the claimant's 1,500 less 200 treated as earned income under regulation 62, plus a partner's 400: 1,700; no partner: 1,300.
#ASSERT `reg 54A(6) — total earned income` 1500 (JUST 400) 200 EQUALS 1700
#ASSERT `reg 54A(6) — total earned income` 1500 NOTHING 200 EQUALS 1300

§ `Regulation 64 -- gainful self-employment`

GIVEN determined IS A BOOLEAN
      main IS A BOOLEAN
      earnings IS A BOOLEAN
      organised IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Claimant who may be in gainful self-employment`
`test gainful claimant` determined main earnings organised MEANS
    `Claimant who may be in gainful self-employment` WITH
        `the Secretary of State has determined the matters in sub-paragraphs (a) to (c)` IS determined
        `the claimant is carrying on a trade, profession or vocation as their main employment` IS main
        `their earnings from that trade, profession or vocation are self-employed earnings` IS earnings
        `the trade, profession or vocation is organised, developed, regular and carried on in expectation of profit` IS organised

#ASSERT `reg 64 — the claimant is in gainful self-employment` (`test gainful claimant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 64 — the claimant is in gainful self-employment` (`test gainful claimant` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 64 — the claimant is in gainful self-employment` (`test gainful claimant` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 64 — the claimant is in gainful self-employment` (`test gainful claimant` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 64 — the claimant is in gainful self-employment` (`test gainful claimant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))

§ `Regulation 63 -- start-up period`

`test March period` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2026 3 5, `last day` IS YMD 2026 4 4

GIVEN previous62 IS A BOOLEAN
      steps IS A BOOLEAN
      earlier IS A BOOLEAN
      began IS A MAYBE DATE
      different IS A BOOLEAN
      terminated IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Start-up period considered under regulation 63`
`test start-up` previous62 steps earlier began different terminated MEANS
    `Start-up period considered under regulation 63` WITH
        `assessment period in which the Secretary of State determines that the claimant is in gainful self-employment` IS `test March period`
        `regulation 62 has previously applied to the claimant in relation to the trade, profession or vocation which is currently the claimant's main employment` IS previous62
        `the claimant is taking active steps to increase their earnings from that employment to the level of the claimant's individual threshold` IS steps
        `a start-up period has previously applied in relation to the claimant` IS earlier
        `date on which that previous start-up period began` IS began
        `that previous start-up period applied in relation to a different trade, profession or vocation which the claimant has ceased to carry on` IS different
        `date on which the Secretary of State terminated the start-up period` IS terminated

GIVEN startup IS A MAYBE `Start-up period`
GIVETH A DATE
`test the first day of` startup MEANS
    CONSIDER startup
    WHEN JUST p THEN p's `first day of the start-up period`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN YMD 1900 1 1

GIVEN startup IS A MAYBE `Start-up period`
GIVETH A DATE
`test the last day of` startup MEANS
    CONSIDER startup
    WHEN JUST p THEN p's `last day of the start-up period`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN YMD 1900 1 1

-- (1): neither regulation 62 nor a start-up period before, and active steps: a start-up period applies.
#ASSERT `reg 63(1) — a start-up period applies` (`test start-up` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 63(1) — a start-up period applies` (`test start-up` TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 63(1) — a start-up period applies` (`test start-up` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING))
-- It runs 12 months from the first day of the assessment period (5 March 2026) to 4 March 2027.
#ASSERT `test the first day of` (`reg 63 — the start-up period` (`test start-up` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 5
#ASSERT `test the last day of` (`reg 63 — the start-up period` (`test start-up` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING)) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 4
-- (3): the Secretary of State terminates it on 10 September 2026: it ends that day. A termination after the twelve months changes nothing.
#ASSERT `test the last day of` (`reg 63 — the start-up period` (`test start-up` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 9 10)))) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 10
#ASSERT `test the last day of` (`reg 63 — the start-up period` (`test start-up` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1)))) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 4
-- No start-up period when the conditions of (1) fail.
#ASSERT `reg 63 — the start-up period` (`test start-up` TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): an earlier start-up period bars a new one unless it began more than 5 years before 5 March 2026 and was for a different trade now ceased.
#ASSERT `reg 63(1) — a start-up period applies` (`test start-up` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 4)) TRUE NOTHING)
-- Began 5 March 2021: exactly five years before, not more than: barred. Began 4 March 2021: more than five years: not barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 63(1) — a start-up period applies` (`test start-up` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2021 3 5)) TRUE NOTHING))
#ASSERT `reg 63(1) — a start-up period applies` (`test start-up` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2021 3 4)) TRUE NOTHING)
-- Long enough ago but for the same trade or one the claimant still carries on: barred. No date for the earlier one: barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 63(1) — a start-up period applies` (`test start-up` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 4)) FALSE NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 63(1) — a start-up period applies` (`test start-up` FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING TRUE NOTHING))

§ `Regulation 62 -- minimum income floor`

-- (4): the net amount of a threshold: 1,000 less 100 for income tax and national insurance contributions is 900.
#ASSERT `reg 62(4) — the net amount of a threshold` 1000 100 EQUALS 900

GIVEN gainful IS A BOOLEAN
      group IS A `Work-related group`
      basis IS A `Claim basis`
      own IS A NUMBER
      partner IS A NUMBER
      surplus IS A NUMBER
      period IS AN `Assessment period`
      startup IS A MAYBE `Start-up period`
GIVETH A `Claimant considered under regulation 62`
`test floor claimant` gainful group basis own partner surplus period startup MEANS
    `Claimant considered under regulation 62` WITH
        `claimant in gainful self-employment` IS gainful
        `work-related group the claimant would fall within, apart from regulation 62 or regulation 90` IS group
        `basis of the claim` IS basis
        `earned income of the claimant for the assessment period` IS own
        `earned income of the claimant's partner for the assessment period` IS partner
        `individual threshold (regulation 90(2))` IS 1000
        `couple threshold (regulation 90(3))` IS 1600
        `amount for income tax and national insurance contributions that the Secretary of State considers appropriate to deduct from the individual threshold` IS 100
        `amount for income tax and national insurance contributions that the Secretary of State considers appropriate to deduct from the couple threshold` IS 160
        `surplus earnings treated as earned income under regulation 54A` IS surplus
        `assessment period` IS period
        `start-up period` IS startup

-- Net thresholds: individual 900, couple 1,440.
`test a single claimant` own surplus MEANS `test floor claimant` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` own 0 surplus `test March period` NOTHING
`test a joint claimant` own partner surplus MEANS `test floor claimant` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `joint claimants` own partner surplus `test March period` NOTHING

#ASSERT `reg 62(4) — the claimant's net individual threshold` (`test a single claimant` 0 0) EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `reg 62(4) — the net couple threshold` (`test a single claimant` 0 0) EQUALS 1440

-- (1): a gainful self-employed claimant who would otherwise be subject to all work-related requirements.
#ASSERT `reg 62(1) — this regulation applies to the claimant` (`test a single claimant` 500 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 62(1) — this regulation applies to the claimant` (`test floor claimant` FALSE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 500 0 0 `test March period` NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 62(1) — this regulation applies to the claimant` (`test floor claimant` TRUE `subject to work-preparation requirement` `a single claimant` 500 0 0 `test March period` NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 62(1) — this regulation applies to the claimant` (`test floor claimant` TRUE `subject to no work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 500 0 0 `test March period` NOTHING))

-- (2): a single claimant with earned income below the individual threshold is treated as having 900; at or above it, the actual.
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a single claimant` 500 0) EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a single claimant` 899.99 0) EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a single claimant` 900 0) EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a single claimant` 1200 0) EQUALS 1200
-- Not within regulation 62(1): the actual earned income.
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test floor claimant` FALSE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 500 0 0 `test March period` NOTHING) EQUALS 500

-- (3): a member of a couple, earned income 500 and a partner's 700: both below the thresholds (500 < 900; 1,200 < 1,440). Treated as
-- 900 - (900 + 700 - 1,440 = 160) = 740; together with the partner, 1,440, the couple threshold.
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a joint claimant` 500 700 0) EQUALS 740
-- A partner with 300: 900 + 300 - 1,440 is negative, so no reduction: the full 900.
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a joint claimant` 500 300 0) EQUALS 900
-- A partner with 1,000: the combined 1,500 is not less than the couple threshold: the actual 500.
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a joint claimant` 500 1000 0) EQUALS 500
-- Exactly at the couple threshold (940 + 500 = 1,440): not less, so actual. Own earned income not below the individual threshold: actual.
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a joint claimant` 500 940 0) EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a joint claimant` 900 100 0) EQUALS 900
-- A single claimant who is a member of a couple gets the couple formula.
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test floor claimant` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` 500 700 0 `test March period` NOTHING) EQUALS 740

-- (4A): surplus earnings of 200 are added first. A single claimant with 500 + 200 = 700 is still below 900: treated as 900.
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a single claimant` 500 200) EQUALS 900
-- 800 + 200 = 1,000 is not below 900: treated as having 1,000.
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a single claimant` 800 200) EQUALS 1000
-- Joint claimants, earned income 500 and 100, surplus 100: added to the claimant it is absorbed by the floor (900 and a combined 1,000);
-- added to the partner the combined is 1,100. The claimant takes it.
#ASSERT `reg 62(4A) — the earned income the claimant is treated as having, with surplus earnings added to one member` (`test a joint claimant` 500 100 100) TRUE EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `reg 62(4A) — the earned income the claimant is treated as having, with surplus earnings added to one member` (`test a joint claimant` 500 100 100) FALSE EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `reg 62(4A) — the surplus earnings are added to the claimant` (`test a joint claimant` 500 100 100)
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a joint claimant` 500 100 100) EQUALS 900
-- A tie (earned income 500, partner 700, surplus 300): added to the claimant the combined is 800 + 700 = 1,500; to the partner, 500 + 1,000; the claimant takes it.
#ASSERT `reg 62(4A) — the surplus earnings are added to the claimant` (`test a joint claimant` 500 700 300)
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test a joint claimant` 500 700 300) EQUALS 800
-- A single claimant is always the one it is added to.
#ASSERT `reg 62(4A) — the surplus earnings are added to the claimant` (`test a single claimant` 500 200)

-- (5): the assessment period 5 March to 4 April 2026 is excluded if it falls wholly within a start-up period, or begins or ends in one.
`test start-up from` first last MEANS `Start-up period` WITH `first day of the start-up period` IS first, `last day of the start-up period` IS last
`test an excluded claimant` startup MEANS `test floor claimant` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 500 0 0 `test March period` (JUST startup)

#ASSERT `reg 62(5) — the assessment period is within or touches a start-up period` (`test an excluded claimant` (`test start-up from` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2027 1 9)))
#ASSERT `reg 62(5) — the assessment period is within or touches a start-up period` (`test an excluded claimant` (`test start-up from` (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10)))
#ASSERT `reg 62(5) — the assessment period is within or touches a start-up period` (`test an excluded claimant` (`test start-up from` (YMD 2026 4 1) (YMD 2027 3 31)))
-- A start-up period that ended the day before the assessment period began, or begins the day after it ended, does not touch it.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 62(5) — the assessment period is within or touches a start-up period` (`test an excluded claimant` (`test start-up from` (YMD 2025 3 5) (YMD 2026 3 4))))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 62(5) — the assessment period is within or touches a start-up period` (`test an excluded claimant` (`test start-up from` (YMD 2026 4 5) (YMD 2027 4 4))))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 62(5) — the assessment period is within or touches a start-up period` (`test a single claimant` 500 0))
-- In such a period the floor does not apply: the actual 500. Outside it, the floor: 900.
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test an excluded claimant` (`test start-up from` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2027 1 9))) EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `reg 62 — the earned income the claimant is treated as having for the assessment period` (`test an excluded claimant` (`test start-up from` (YMD 2025 3 5) (YMD 2026 3 4))) EQUALS 900
